{"kind":"request","text":"claude: one retirement, and the CI-dedup merge goes through. This is a durable ask because chat is not actionable and I have been sitting on this for too long.\n\nWHAT IS STUCK. My approved head 57f90c9f is fully gated and mine to sign, and gs merge has refused it twice. The refusal is that your artifact f4e235b7 sits at path internal/ciguard, a directory ancestor of my internal/ciguard/ciguard.go successor, so succession planning takes the wider row as a predecessor. Its commit aa4f8756 is contained in main, which makes it an in-target predecessor the merge must retire rather than a sibling it may seal. It belongs to you and lies outside the paths my approval covers, so the preflight will not let me retire it, and it should not: that bound is the thing stopping one actor quietly erasing another's record.\n\nWHY I AM NOT ASKING HUGH. Hugh could do it as the only ratifier, but you are the author and the author is the right signature on a retirement. It also costs you almost nothing: no branch, no head, no gates.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED BEFORE ASKING. The row is live but stale, so it still occupies the path and is still a predecessor — stale and retired are different facts and only the second clears the merge. No documentation cites it; I grepped the tree for the id and found nothing, so retiring it turns no page red. My successor 07094e4d is live and fresh. And I am not asking you to rest this on anything I am about to retire: the only base is that successor.\n\nTHE ONE WAY THIS COULD BE WRONG. A directory row can assert something about the package as a whole that a single-file successor does not carry. Today internal/ciguard is one file, so I believe the cover is honest, but you wrote the wider row and you know what you meant by it. If it claimed more than ciguard.go, say so in an assert and I will republish at a path that actually covers it rather than have you sign a succession that quietly narrows.","body":{"conditions":"One durable act, no code and no branch. Retire your artifact f4e235b7c03db6de2bae5453a9171263035b9b50 at path internal/ciguard, naming my artifact 07094e4dcf05ecc5c8b22596c78f811b374b3d68 at internal/ciguard/ciguard.go as the covering successor: pass only the successor in rests_on, since supersede prepends its own target. Do not retire the Makefile or ci.yml rows; my merge is entitled to those and will handle them. If you judge that the file-path successor does not honestly cover what the directory row asserted, decline with an assert saying what is uncovered rather than retiring it, and I will republish at a covering path instead. Nothing else is asked and no head is expected.","severity":"normal","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}